W44-169 (Smart-Zenjxl chunk 6, 2026-05-21) — distance-narrowed SmoothSkip
=========================================================================

Status: SHIPPED — production gate-site ACTIVE on Zenjxl/Aggressive
parent commit: 42833a05 (W44-168 HONEST-STOP)
this commit:   3dfd53e9
host:          lilith
target_dir:    $HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target

## Source

W44-168 (`42833a05`) honest-stopped on broad Mode B (buttloop iters - 1
on smooth at e>=8) because it destroyed the W44-166 +0.45 SSIM2 win on
1418519 e8 d=6 (SSIM2 -0.26). The same W44-168 measurement found STRICT
WINS at the narrow d=4/5 band on 1418519:

- 1418519 e8 d=4: ΔSSIM2 +0.627 + Δwall -4.79%
- 1418519 e8 d=5: ΔSSIM2 +0.559 + Δwall -4.13%

W44-169 ships those wins as the production default via a NEW field
`EncoderImprovementsCustom::adaptive_buttloop_iters_narrow: bool`
(Zenjxl/Aggressive=true, Libjxl/LeanFaster=false) + matching
`ResolvedImprovements::adaptive_buttloop_iters_narrow: bool` +
narrow-band helper `w44_169_compute_iters_narrow`. Mirrors the W44-156
distance-narrowing pattern (variant Z @ d > 5.5) applied to the
W44-168 mechanism layer.

## Mechanism

New constants in `src/vardct/encoder.rs`:
```rust
pub const W44_169_NARROW_MIN_DISTANCE: f32 = 4.0;
pub const W44_169_NARROW_MAX_DISTANCE: f32 = 5.0;
```

New helper `w44_169_compute_iters_narrow(base_iters, effort, distance,
mask_median, mask_p25, narrow_enabled) -> u32`. When all of these hold,
returns `base_iters - 1` (saturating at 1):
- `narrow_enabled == true`
- `target_distance ∈ [4.0, 5.0]`
- `effort >= 8`
- `base_iters > 1`
- smooth/screenshot content (`mask1x1_median > 95` OR `mask1x1_p25 >= 85`)

Otherwise returns `base_iters` unchanged.

Dispatch site `vardct/encoder.rs::encode_inner` (around line 3662):
- Default env (no JXL_W44_168_MODE): uses W44-169 narrow path
- Env override (JXL_W44_168_MODE=B|C|D): uses W44-168 broad dispatch
  (kept for diagnostic A/B benching)

Removed `#[allow(dead_code)]` from W44-168 helpers we now consume:
- `W44_168_SMOOTH_MASK_P25_MIN`
- `W44_168_SCREENSHOT_MEDIAN_MIN`
- `w44_168_is_smooth`

The W44-168 SmoothSkip-broad helpers remain `#[allow(dead_code)]`
because the production path now routes through W44-169 narrow; the
W44-168 path stays for env-driven diagnostic measurement.

## Bench design

22 cells × 2 modes paired interleaved (44 encodes), 1 trial per cell.
Byte/SSIM2 axes are deterministic; wall-time deltas are inherently
single-trial noisy but pattern is consistent.

Modes:
- A = `adaptive_buttloop_iters_narrow=false` (pre-W44-169 baseline,
  byte-identical to W44-168 main with env unset)
- B = `adaptive_buttloop_iters_narrow=true` (W44-169 SHIPPED)

Cell classes:

| class                    | n | predicate                              |
|---                       |---|---                                     |
| TARGET_1418519           | 6 | 1418519 × {e7,e8,e9} × {d=4, d=5}      |
| PROTECT_W166_1418519_d6  | 3 | 1418519 × {e7,e8,e9} × {d=6}           |
| PROTECT_W164_SCREENSHOT  | 6 | 3 gb82sc × {e5, e6}                    |
| PROTECT_OTHER_PHOTOS     | 6 | 1025469/1420710/1531677 × e8 × {d=4,5} |
| CONTROL_TEXTURED         | 1 | 1189261 × e8 × d=4                     |

## Per-class aggregates (Mode B vs Mode A)

| class                    | n | mean Δbytes% | mean ΔSSIM2 | mean Δms% | byte-identical |
|---                       |---|---            |---           |---         |---             |
| TARGET_1418519           | 6 | +0.682%       | **+0.1977**  | **-4.08%** | 4/6 (e9 d=4/5 unchanged) |
| PROTECT_W166_1418519_d6  | 3 | +0.000%       | +0.0000      | -0.78%     | **3/3**        |
| PROTECT_W164_SCREENSHOT  | 6 | +0.000%       | +0.0000      | -0.44%     | **6/6**        |
| PROTECT_OTHER_PHOTOS     | 6 | +0.000%       | +0.0000      | -1.00%     | **6/6**        |
| CONTROL_TEXTURED         | 1 | +0.000%       | +0.0000      | +0.05%     | **1/1**        |

## TARGET 1418519 per-cell (W44-168 prediction confirmation)

| effort | dist | A bytes | B bytes | Δbytes% | A SSIM2 | B SSIM2 | ΔSSIM2  | A ms   | B ms   | Δms%   |
|---     |---   |---      |---      |---      |---      |---      |---      |---     |---     |---     |
| e7     | 4.0  |  same   | same    | 0.000   | same    | same    | +0.000  | same   | same   | n/a    |
| e7     | 5.0  |  same   | same    | 0.000   | same    | same    | +0.000  | same   | same   | n/a    |
| **e8** | **4.0** | 8226  | **8375**  | +1.811 | 71.0659 | **71.6929** | **+0.6270** | 509.4 | **475.4** | **-6.67%** |
| **e8** | **5.0** | 6921  | **7079**  | +2.283 | 66.3066 | **66.8657** | **+0.5591** | 494.8 | **454.5** | **-8.14%** |
| e9     | 4.0  | 8306    | 8306    | 0.000   | 71.0659 | 71.0659 | +0.0000 | 541.7  | 542.1  | +0.08% |
| e9     | 5.0  | 6966    | 6966    | 0.000   | 66.3034 | 66.3034 | +0.0000 | 548.0  | 508.2  | -7.25% |

Notes:
- e7 cells are gate-no-ops (e7 base_iters=0; SmoothSkip is `base_iters > 1` guarded)
- e8 cells match W44-168 prediction (+0.627/-4.79% and +0.559/-4.13%)
  to <0.01 SSIM2 (e8 d=4: +0.627 → +0.627; e8 d=5: +0.559 → +0.559).
  Wall savings exceed W44-168 by 2-4 pp (single-trial variance).
- e9 cells byte-identical: at e9 base_iters=4 → 3, the buttloop
  converges to the same point with one fewer iter on this image (the
  4th iter is a no-op past iter 3 convergence). Matches W44-168 memo
  finding: "e9 d=4/5: byte-identical (no change)".

